{"name":"Pixie Dust","hex":"#f6d5dc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pixie dust","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of fairy dust."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pixie_dust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tinker Bell","blocks":[{"text":"Tinker Bell is a fictional character from J. M. Barrie's 1904 play Peter Pan and its 1911 novelisation Peter and Wendy. She has appeared in a variety of film and television adaptations of the Peter Pan stories, in particular the 1953 animated Walt Disney picture Peter Pan. She also appears in the official 2006 sequel Peter Pan in Scarlet by Geraldine McCaughrean commissioned by Great Ormond Street Hospital as well as the Peter and the Starcatchers book series by Ridley Pearson and Dave Barry."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/42/Tinkclose-1-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tinker_Bell","wikidata":"Q853847"},{"title":"Pixie","blocks":[{"text":"A pixie is a mythical creature of British folklore. Pixies are speculated to be particularly concentrated in the high moorland areas around Cornwall and Devon, suggesting some Celtic origin for the belief and name. However, the word 'pixie' also appears in Dorset, Somerset and to a lesser extent in Sussex, Wiltshire and Hampshire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Page_83_illustration_in_More_English_Fairy_Tales.png/330px-Page_83_illustration_in_More_English_Fairy_Tales.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pixie","wikidata":"Q1144339"},{"title":"Dust","blocks":[{"text":"Dust is made of fine particles of solid matter. On Earth, it generally consists of particles in the atmosphere that come from various sources such as soil lifted by wind, volcanic eruptions, and pollution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/co